# Root priority audit — PR110

Status: in progress. Source and mathematical audit100%; no priority or publication clearance. Target is literal unprimed k603, the equality of ordinary focal-to-antipedal-vertex distance sums for all admissible closed elliptic-caustic billiard periods and windings. Original head3d159f0a00d0bd7ff8d558d6fbc75af5094f7a35; original effort2/5; new central proof-search turns0.

## Primary sources inspected

The authenticated 2020 arXiv source2004.12497v11 and published 2021 companion (DOI10.1007/s40598-021-00174-y) define q* as ordinary Euclidean norms and list k603 with allN, ratio1, and an unresolved proof marker. Root inspected the complete relevant definitions and tables, including rendered Figure3 and Table7. This establishes the historical conjecture and its target, not its current novelty.

Ronaldo Garcia, Dan Reznik, Hellmuth Stachel, and Mark Helman, *Steiner’s Hat: a Constant-Area Deltoid Associated with the Ellipse*, arXiv2006.13166v5, revised5October2020, related journal DOI10.31896/k.24.2. Root fully read the extracted25-page body, including all theorems, appendices and bibliography. Root rendered and visually inspected page3 with the precise continuous antipedal definition and Lemma1. The current arXiv metadata comments say23pages, while the downloaded actual PDF has25; the actual file takes precedence.

This paper gives continuous negative-pedal envelopes, area invariance for a reference point on the outer ellipse, cusp triangles, osculating-circle relations, and orthology. Its general envelope construction solves L(t)=L'(t)=0. The finite antipedal vertex in PR110 instead solves L(t_i)=L(t_{i+1})=0 for a chord tangent to a fixed nondegenerate inner confocal ellipse. The paper's Poncelet triangles use the half-scale Steiner inellipse; for a>b, that pair is not confocal. No theorem in this inspected body establishes the equality of the two finite ordinary focal radial-distance sums. Envelope or area invariance alone therefore does not supply a covering result. This conclusion concerns this exact inspected version; it does not certify all historical negative-pedal literature.

The journal-hosted download at https://hrcak.srce.hr/file/361574 returned HTTP418 in both the web tool and actual curl child18574. The accessible alternate primary arXiv PDF was downloaded by child19881; actual extraction20029, pdfinfo20030 and page3render21210 succeeded. The failed journal download is preserved as a failure, not cited as a full journal-body read.

## Search coverage and limits

Root queried exact k603, focal antipedal, antipedal focal distance, sum/ellipse/focus, Poncelet and theorem variants. Results returned the original source, its author experimental video ledger, modern bicentric geometry, continuous negative-pedal work and nearby2026 area/centroid preprints. Search absence is only a discovery aid. Every candidate must be read at theorem level before a priority conclusion. Nonprimary snippets and unrelated keyword collisions are not evidence.

Three fresh independent families are checking the exact conjecture history, classical confocal mechanisms and modern general invariants. Their interim messages are not completed reports. Root has not yet used them as priority clearance. The modern spatial-integral manuscript arXiv2102.10899 is a legitimate precursor of DOI10.1007/s10883-022-09608-y; a precursor read must be distinguished from its later journal version. Its relevance is under independent review. Metadata, citation indexes and abstracts are not substitutes for essential full theorem bodies.

No prior covering proof has yet been established by root. Substantive novelty remains a hypothesis pending all sealed families, full root report reads and any necessary cross-adjudication. No paper, DOI, tracker write, native change or PR110 merge is authorised by this interim record.


